Aboutbox.mcc/Aboutbox.mcc

    NAME
        Aboutbox.mcc -- Display application information and credits.

    SUPERCLASS
        Window.mui

    DESCRIPTION
        Build a window with a logo, a scrolling information/credits area, and
        an Ok button. The source configuration declares version 20.30. All
        five Aboutbox attributes are initialization-only, with no local
        setters or getters. Constructor duplicates use the last value.
        During Window_Setup, read Application_Title, Description, Version, and
        Copyright. Show the title in bold and append description and version.
        Strip an initial literal "$VER: " from the version string; no
        version/date parser or author-list parser is implemented. Append build
        text beneath a non-NULL Application_Version, then prepend the literal
        English "Copyright " to the copyright value.
        The title bar becomes "About " plus Application_Title, limited by a
        128-byte buffer. Provide a non-NULL application title and a non-NULL
        Credits string, even when the latter is empty: setup formats the title
        and unconditionally dereferences Credits. Missing Credits is not
        safely treated as no credits.
        Ok and CloseRequest queue Window_Open FALSE through
        Application_PushMethod. Attach the object to its Application and
        follow the normal Window lifecycle. The class does not open itself.

    NOTES
        Build, Credits, LogoFile, and LogoData pointers are borrowed at
        construction. Keep their storage valid for subsequent setup/open
        cycles; constructor return does not end their lifetime requirement.
        Generated app-info and expanded credits buffers are owned by the
        object and freed at disposal. Cleanup removes and disposes the
        per-setup logo and clears generated text for reuse.
        Credits appear below a divider in the same scrolling area, not on a
        second page. Build information is not hidden behind a version-number
        click. Placeholder labels and the About/Copyright/Ok text are
        hard-coded English. No ABOUTBOX_DEBUG environment-variable handler
        exists in this implementation.
        Buffer-growth failure can silently leave partial or truncated text;
        setup still returns superclass success. Logo fallback stops at the
        first non-NULL object, not at verified successful image rendering.
        This reference makes no MorphOS-specific path, size, or localization
        claims.

    SEE ALSO
        MUIA_Aboutbox_Build, MUIA_Aboutbox_Credits,
        MUIA_Aboutbox_LogoFallbackMode
Aboutbox.mcc/MUIA_Aboutbox_Build

    NAME
        MUIA_Aboutbox_Build -- Append build information to the version text.

    FUNCTION
        Store a borrowed build string for later information generation.

    INPUTS
        Initialize only; STRPTR to a NUL-terminated string, or NULL. Default
        NULL. No local setter or getter.

    NOTES
        Displayed on a new line after Application_Version when that
        application attribute is non-NULL. It is visible without clicking.
        Without a version string, Build is not appended. No format parsing or
        source-control integration occurs. Keep the string valid across setup
        cycles; it is not copied at construction.
Aboutbox.mcc/MUIA_Aboutbox_Credits

    NAME
        MUIA_Aboutbox_Credits -- Supply credits text with placeholders.

    FUNCTION
        Store a borrowed credits string and expand it during setup.

    INPUTS
        Initialize only; non-NULL readable NUL-terminated string. Use an empty
        string for no credits. No local setter or getter.

    NOTES
        The instance defaults to a NULL pointer, but ParseCredits dereferences
        it unconditionally. Supply this attribute explicitly with valid
        storage that remains alive across setup cycles. Credits are shown in
        the same scrolling area as application information.
        Each tab expands to four spaces. %% produces a percent sign. Unknown
        %x sequences retain x and drop the percent; a trailing percent is
        dropped. Other bytes, including MUI text escapes, pass to the Text
        object without encoding conversion. The expansion starts with a
        newline.
        Placeholders expand to fixed English text:
        %p Programming:; %P Additional programming:; %l Translations:; %L
        Proofreading:; %t Thanks to:; %T Special thanks to:.
        %a Acknowledgements:; %d Documentation:; %i Icons:; %I Icon:; %W Web
        support:; %m Music:; %s Sound effects:; %g Graphics:; %? Disclaimer:;
        %$ License:.
        No localization lookup or line-length enforcement occurs. Expansion
        allocation failure has no explicit error result.

    EXAMPLE
        MUIA_Aboutbox_Credits, (IPTR)"%p\n\tExample Author"
Aboutbox.mcc/MUIA_Aboutbox_LogoData

    NAME
        MUIA_Aboutbox_LogoData -- Supply embedded logo data.

    FUNCTION
        Store a borrowed Rawimage payload for the I fallback step.

    INPUTS
        Initialize only; const struct MUI_RawimageData *, or NULL. Default
        NULL. No local setter or getter.

    NOTES
        When the fallback order reaches I, non-NULL data is passed to a
        Rawimage object. That class defines the format, byte order, validity
        requirements, and borrowed payload lifetime. Keep the image valid
        throughout use and later setup cycles. There is no local 64-by-64 size
        check or resizing rule.
        Unsupported data may make Rawimage construction fail and allow a later
        fallback step. A non-NULL logo object ends fallback; no rendered-image
        verification follows. NULL skips this step.

    SEE ALSO
        MUIA_Aboutbox_LogoFallbackMode, Rawimage.mcc/MUIA_Rawimage_Data
Aboutbox.mcc/MUIA_Aboutbox_LogoFallbackMode

    NAME
        MUIA_Aboutbox_LogoFallbackMode -- Set the logo search order.

    FUNCTION
        Choose the sequence of logo-object construction attempts.

    INPUTS
        Initialize only; ULONG. Default MUIV_Aboutbox_LogoFallbackMode_Auto,
        MAKE_ID('D', 'E', 'I', 0). NoLogo (0) disables attempts. No local
        setter or getter.

    NOTES
        Process bytes from most significant to least significant until a zero
        byte, exhausted value, or non-NULL logo. D creates a private icon
        object from the program name. E tries LogoFile through Dtpic after
        checking that the path names a file. I tries LogoData through
        Rawimage. Unknown nonzero bytes are skipped.
        D uses GetProgramName when available, rewrites an APPDIR: name as
        PROGDIR: plus its file part, or constructs PROGDIR: plus the task name
        when GetProgramName fails. It is not unconditionally
        PROGDIR:<executable>.info. Paths use fixed internal buffers.
        Success means object creation, not proof of decoded/rendered image
        content. The actual public attribute is LogoFallbackMode; the older
        document's LogoFallback name is not defined in the AROS header.

    EXAMPLE
        MUIA_Aboutbox_LogoFallbackMode, MAKE_ID('D', 'I', 0, 0)

    SEE ALSO
        MUIA_Aboutbox_LogoFile, MUIA_Aboutbox_LogoData
Aboutbox.mcc/MUIA_Aboutbox_LogoFile

    NAME
        MUIA_Aboutbox_LogoFile -- Supply a file for the E fallback step.

    FUNCTION
        Store a borrowed path used to construct a Dtpic logo.

    INPUTS
        Initialize only; readable NUL-terminated STRPTR, or NULL. Default
        NULL. No local setter or getter.

    NOTES
        When E is reached, Lock/Examine must identify a file rather than a
        directory. The path is then supplied as MUIA_Dtpic_Name. NULL or a
        failed file check skips the attempt. Relative paths are not explicitly
        rejected; their interpretation follows the task's DOS context.
        The wrapper imposes no 64-by-64 size limit and no MorphOS volume
        requirement. Image loading and display follow Dtpic. A non-NULL Dtpic
        object stops fallback before later setup/rendering success is known.
        Keep the path valid for all relevant setup cycles.

    SEE ALSO
        MUIA_Aboutbox_LogoFallbackMode
